      "Edge and hosting choices are open, so where TLS terminates and which third parties can see plaintext is undecided.",
      "TLS from clients terminates at the managed edge, which is operated by the hosting or edge provider and listed as a subservice organization. Traffic from the edge to the application is re-encrypted with TLS and certificate verification; no hop carries donor PII or credentials in cleartext. The set of parties that can observe decrypted request content (edge provider, WAF, the application) is documented in the system description. Bank account numbers and other restricted fields are additionally protected by field-level encryption at the application (ANS-ENC-008), so edge logging cannot capture them in reusable form if request logging is disabled for those paths. Edge request body logging is off by default.",
